# What to commit from .ground/ — convention shared with other ground projects.
#
# TRACK (source of truth, by omission below):
#   truth/chain.jsonl        the axiom chain
#   mem/chain.jsonl          the belief chain
#   axiom-bindings.json      declared intent ↔ code bindings (agentics-specific)
#   meta.json                world name
#   ilx/model.ilx            the semantic graph — source, like the chains
#   ilx/metrics.jsonl        the measured time series; declared figures cite it
#   .gitignore               this file
#
# IGNORE (derived, transient, or local working state):
truth/world.json
truth/chain.wal
truth/cursors.json
truth/rejections.jsonl
mem/chain.wal
mem/cursors.json
mem/graph.json
# Rebuildable from the tracked chains — including promotion links, which are
# re-derived from the axioms' `[promoted from MEM-x]` markers on the truth
# chain (`ground mem graph rebuild`, or `ground doctor --fix`). Before that
# derivation existed, a promotion lived ONLY here and a fresh clone lost it.
mem/graph.db
mem/graph.db-shm
mem/graph.db-wal
# Derived: always rebuildable from model.ilx + the chain, never authoritative.
ilx/index.json
# Pending proposals (`ground ilx propose`). model.ilx is the source of truth; a
# delta is a document ABOUT a change that has not happened, and the record of one
# that did is the approval on the flow queue plus the model file itself.
ilx/deltas/
# Derived: which nodes a delta has moved under since their check last passed.
# `node-bindings.json` beside it IS tracked — a node's check is authored intent
# about the projection, like a recipe's Status line.
ilx/built.json
flow/
plan/
journal/
harness/
# The agent's runtime state: pi's session transcripts, its model store, the
# models.json ground writes for it — and `auth.json`, which is a CREDENTIAL and
# must never be committed (AX-AGENTICS-00101 puts it in the world precisely so
# it is not machine-global; that is not an argument for it being in git).
agent/

# The factory's working state (AX-AGENTICS-00078): run checkpoints, level logs
# and generated directives. Derived from a plan and reproducible by re-running
# it — and previously written into the harness crate's SOURCE directory, which
# is how a build came to dirty tracked code.
work/runs
work/directives

# work/recipes is NOT ignored: a recipe library is authored intent, like the
# chains, and a `bless` that changes its Status line is a decision worth
# reviewing.

# Derived: verdicts recorded against the fingerprint that produced them.
verify-cache.json
verify-cache.json.tmp

# Derived: what `ground next` last said, for the status line, and what the
# Handoff mod last saw. Both are worked out again from the world on the next read.
next.json
next.json.tmp
mods/
# What turns left for db, waiting to be accepted or rejected (`ground propose`):
# this machine's working state, like the plan.
harvest/
